    "text": "1 days ago -0- State Representative Ben DeSmidt has been selected as Kenosha Labor Person of the year. The Kenosha AFL-CIO Council announced their selection Tuesday night. DeSmidt is a former Carthage College professor who now co-owns Union Park Tavern in Kenosha. He'll be formally recognized during Laborfest to be held Monday--Labor Day--at Pennoyer Park on the city's north side. As was the case last year, the event will be held in conjunction with labor organizations from Racine. The event is open to the public and runs from 11 to 4. Read full article\n1",
